.TH AGENTSTACK 1 "2026-09-20" "AgentStack" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agentstack \- control the AgentStack per-user service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agentstack
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
AgentStack is installed as a session-scoped systemd user service. It never
enables linger and package installation does not start or enable the service.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B enable [--now]
Reload this user's systemd manager and enable AgentStack. With
.B --now
also start it.
.TP
.B start | stop | restart
Manage this user's AgentStack service.
.TP
.B status [--json]
Report unit and local control-socket health without starting the service.
.TP
.B logs [--component COMPONENT] [--follow]
Read this user's AgentStack journal entries.
.TP
.B doctor [--json]
Report prerequisites and remedies without changing the machine.
.TP
.B daemon
Run the daemon in the foreground for development or service execution.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/agentstack/releases/<version>
Immutable installed release payload.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/agentstack/current
Package-managed link to the installed release.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/agentstack
Private, session-scoped runtime directory.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/agentstack
User configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/agentstack
User durable state, including separate engine homes.
.SH NOTES
For package upgrades, use the documented stop, upgrade, start sequence. The
package never changes user configuration or state on install, remove, or purge.
